## selftest

honest switch onto 52 SOL at lambda 50.00 %: L_ema/sqrt(XY) 1.000 at the adoption, 1.000 at the gate (+9 s); P_ema/P 1.000; box wide 0 s in the warm-up, 0 s after; guard cleared at +9 s
honest switch onto 150 SOL at lambda 99.78 %: L_ema/sqrt(XY) 1.995 at the adoption, 1.000 at the gate (+9 s); P_ema/P 1.000; box wide 4 s in the warm-up, 0 s after; guard cleared at +9 s
honest switch onto 240 SOL at lambda 25.00 %: L_ema/sqrt(XY) 0.500 at the adoption, 1.000 at the gate (+9 s); P_ema/P 1.000; box wide 4 s in the warm-up, 0 s after; guard cleared at +9 s
gate: a genuinely liquidatable position (2.2x) is liquidated at +9 s (the 8th warm-up integration lands at +9 s)

## 1. M4R-1: a lambda 50 % candidate (52 SOL at the pre-halt price) whose every unlocked LP unit the
attacker holds; the position carried from a 100-SOL fully locked AMM v4 (Tier C, cr_liq 1.5).  The
candidate trades at m x the pre-halt price, flat after the adoption.  Every second after the adoption:
the keeper's honest crank and plain liquidation attempt; the attacker's [withdraw all, crank, deposit]
and [withdraw all, liquidate, deposit].  Cells: outcome, k = keeper / a = attacker, seconds after the
adoption, (borrower SOL at the exit, or equity if open).  120 s.  The honest threshold is m 2.01 (the
'none' rows): every earlier exit in a wrapped row is forced.

