## 6. M4R-2: the token dumps f x during the halt; the only candidate has 30 SOL of locked SOL at the
pre-halt price (lambda 99.78 %, D = 30 % of pool_d), i.e. 30/sqrt(f) SOL at the live price (window floor
25 SOL).  Attacker: none / the thin pool's backer pump-wraps the recording proposal back to the frozen
price; or no dump during the halt but a genuine one 5 s into the collection window.  Cells: adopted?; P_ema
vs the candidate's price at the switch (M4R: -> at the gate); real locked SOL at the live price; the
attacker's round-trip cost (engine P).

