### 8d. Atomic price bundles in attacker-only seconds (M4X-1).  Engine W's market; the position's vault
raised by add_margin (+0 / +25 / +50 / +100 % of V) so its honest threshold is about 2-4x the pre-halt
price; the candidate trades FLAT at 1.00x after the adoption.  The keeper is absent for s <= k after the
adoption (degraded mode); every second the attacker sends [buy kc, crank_price, sell] and [buy kl, liquidate,
sell], with its best kc in {1.5 ... 12} and kl in {1.0, 1.1, 1.25, 1.5} x the threshold (the pumped buyback
must still fit V - K_s).  Cells: the earliest forced liquidation, seconds after the adoption (kc, kl), or
open (30 s).  Before M4X-1 the warm-up seed read the pumped low directly: 8 attacker-only seconds forced ANY
threshold at +9 s.  With the step bound the reach is exactly as built's (whose P_ema moves at most
x(tau + dt*(1 + C))/(tau + dt) per integration, the same bound), and never earlier (the gate).

